Food Delivery System

Project

A command-line Food Delivery System developed in Python using Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).

The project models:

Users

Customers

Delivery Partners

Restaurants

Menu Items

Orders

Files

food_delivery.py - Contains all six required class definitions.

demo.py - Runs the complete end-to-end demonstration without input().

README.md - Project instructions.

Requirements

Python 3.x

No external packages are required.

How to Run

Open a terminal in this project folder and run:

python demo.py

The demonstration automatically performs the complete flow:

Registers Priya as a customer.

Registers Rajesh as a delivery partner.

Creates Bawarchi restaurant and its menu.

Tops up Priya's wallet.

Rejects a negative wallet top-up.

Places an order for Biryani and Kebab.

Calculates the bill.

Shows the estimated delivery time.

Rajesh accepts the order.

Tests an incorrect OTP.

Completes delivery with OTP 1234.

Sends customer and delivery-partner notifications.

Runs completion checks.

Expected Bill

For Biryani (Rs. 250) and Kebab (Rs. 180):

Subtotal: Rs. 430.00

GST (5%): Rs. 21.50

Packaging fee: Rs. 20.00

Total: Rs. 471.50

Estimated time: 30 minutes

OOP Concepts Demonstrated

Abstraction using ABC and abstractmethod

Inheritance through Customer and DeliveryPartner

Encapsulation through private/protected attributes

Polymorphism through different notify() implementations

Object interaction between restaurants, menu items, customers, delivery partners, and orders